Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CanonicalMultiwayEvolution", "ObjectName",
 CellID->744232536,ExpressionUUID->"1934bf0f-7a30-534b-b2d6-0717a569bd0e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"af2d1c4d-20d1-a343-abc0-d8d8632d6373"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalMultiwayEvolution",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
CanonicalMultiwayEvolution"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "state", ",", " ", "limits"}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"45548c20-8186-6643-b606-a32716ab6a47"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "explores every rewrite of the rule or rule set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["rule", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ad43a68d-239d-8142-8b7e-fad64db3e4a0"],
 " from the hypergraph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["state", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b4e89322-4ef2-4b45-9703-808b0de5fb64"],
 " breadth first, merging isomorphic states, within the evolution limits ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["limits", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2cae23cb-62aa-9748-9271-bb107c6b7eb3"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalMultiwayEvolution",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
CanonicalMultiwayEvolution"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "state", ",", " ", "limits", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<RecordEvents\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4d8c76f4-0d9e-1042-9cb7-1ea960cd8546"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "also records every raw rewrite event.",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
  "9a35ef1b-4aa0-544e-bc79-b66d2cb5bc9b"]
}], "Usage",
 CellID->989944088,ExpressionUUID->"dde275a3-48c1-b845-bd51-6753b87d922b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "States are identified by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "CanonicalStateForm", 
    "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/CanonicalStateForm",
     "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/SamuelFrerichs/\
StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/CanonicalStateForm.html"},
   "TextRefLink",
   DisplayFunction->(TagBox[
     ButtonBox[
      StyleBox[#, ShowStringCharacters -> True, FontFamily -> 
       "Source Sans Pro"], 
      BaseStyle -> {"Link", FontColor -> LightDarkSwitched[
          RGBColor[0.02, 0.286, 0.651], 
          RGBColor[0.2823, 0.6666, 0.949]]}, ButtonData -> #2, ContentPadding -> 
      False], 
     MouseAppearanceTag["LinkHand"]]& )]],ExpressionUUID->
  "99a5490c-96f0-a844-b669-cb3fab4dcf44"],
 " in the active universe, so the result is a canonical states graph: one \
vertex per isomorphism class reached, one edge per pair of classes joined by \
some rewrite event, with \"TransitionMultiplicities\" counting the raw events \
behind each edge."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->494985747,ExpressionUUID->"4ddbfd77-eb98-8c49-a76c-ae5f7251e311"],

Cell["\<\
Evolution limits are an Association with the keys \"MaxGenerations\" (default \
10), \"MaxEvents\" (1000), \"MaxStates\" (Infinity) and \"TimeConstraint\" \
(30. seconds); missing keys take their defaults.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->883425743,ExpressionUUID->"ce34a0f7-03bf-ab47-9ef5-a32d67018138"],

Cell["\<\
The status is \"Halted\" when the exploration is exhaustive and found no \
cycle: it is verified to halt under this finite reachable exploration. \
\"CycleDetected\" means the explored states graph contains a cycle, so an \
infinite derivation exists; the result then carries a \"CycleWitness\". \
\"GenerationCap\", \"EventCap\", \"StateCap\" and \"TimedOut\" mean the \
exploration was not resolved within the stated limits, and \"Invalid\" means \
a rewrite application failed. A capped exploration never reports its \
unexplored frontier as terminal.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->400878589,ExpressionUUID->"12d5c1db-ed13-e447-bb90-75e4287d22ef"],

Cell["\<\
The result has the keys \"Generations\", \"States\", \"StatesGraph\", \
\"TransitionEdges\", \"TransitionMultiplicities\", \"TerminalStates\", \
\"Frontier\", \"DiscoveryGenerations\", \"Status\", \"CycleDetectedQ\", \
\"CycleWitness\", \"LongestDerivation\", \"LongestDerivationExactQ\", \
\"EventCount\", \"LimitsReached\", \"EvolutionLimits\", \"EventRecords\" and \
\"EvaluatorVersion\".\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->721467504,ExpressionUUID->"e163c074-e391-9041-bba8-5adeb51b0a80"],

Cell["\<\
In a formal model of this breadth-first canonical explorer, machine-checked \
in Lean 4 with Mathlib, a \"Halted\" status implies that every derivation \
from the initial state is finite and shorter than the number of explored \
states, and the longest derivation equals the longest path of the explored \
graph. This holds for a complete, invariant canonical form (the default \
\"Exact\" backend) and also when canonical forms are merely isomorphic copies \
(the \"Native\" backend). That this code implements the model is tested, not \
machine-checked.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->131864767,ExpressionUUID->"3bc488a9-b6e1-0d4f-92be-20e92084ba8c"]
}, Open  ]],

